SPPARKS (18 May 2017)
app_style   cooxidation
seed        1000

dimension   2
boundary    p p p

# Lattice
variable    n1x          equal 300
variable    n1y          equal 300

lattice     sq/4n 1.0
region      sys_domain block 0 ${n1x} 0 ${n1y} -0.5 0.5 # n1x * n1y sites
region      sys_domain block 0 300 0 ${n1y} -0.5 0.5 region      sys_domain block 0 300 0 300 -0.5 0.5 create_box  sys_domain
Created box = (0 0 -0.5) to (300 300 0.5)
  1 by 1 by 1 processor grid
create_sites box
Creating sites ...
  90000 sites
  90000 sites have 4 neighbors

# Setting
variable    Trun   equal 1.0e-12   # time step
variable    nstep  equal 100       # total number of time step
variable    Time   equal ${Trun}*${nstep}
variable    Time   equal 1e-12*${nstep}
variable    Time   equal 1e-12*100
variable    Tstat  equal ${Trun}   # time step for stats
variable    Tstat  equal 1e-12   
solve_style tree
sector      yes tstop ${Trun}
sector      yes tstop 1e-12

temperature 600.

###########################

# i1:       1 (siteA) 2 (siteB) 3 (siteC)
# i2:       0 (vac) 1 (spec1) 2 (spec2) 3 (spec3)
# i3 - i5:  ac1-ac3 = number of adsorption events of the species at the site
# i6 - i8:  dc1-dc3 = number of desoprtion events of the species at the site
# d1 - d3:  pressure1-3 = partial pressure of the fluid cell right above the site 
# d4:       temperature

set         i1 value 1                                 # all siteA
  90000 settings made for i1
set         i2 value 0                                 # all vac
  90000 settings made for i2
set         i2 value 1 fraction 4.959591e-01           # initially equilibrium
  44709 settings made for i2

event       5 siteA siteA vac   vac   1.041370e+08 spec1 spec1 # adsorption of spec1 (rate)
event       6 siteA siteA spec1 spec1 1.075585e+08 vac   vac   # desorption of spec1

###########################

stats       ${Tstat}
stats       1e-12

diag_style  cooxidation stats yes list vac spec1 B1 E1
# vac, spec1: number of vacancy, species 1
# B1, E1: number of events (adsorption, desorption)

run ${Time} pre no post no
run 1e-10 pre no post no
